pve-console-wall (1.0.13) stable; urgency=medium

  * Console now fills the whole tile (width and height). noVNC's Local Scaling
    is a "contain" fit that left black bars and never used the full tile width.
    Replace it with pure CSS (object-fit: cover) on the noVNC canvas, which
    covers the tile at any size, adapts automatically on resize, and keeps
    aspect ratio (slight crop). noVNC's own scaling is turned off so it does not
    fight the CSS. Trade-off: interactive cursor mapping may be slightly off on
    covered consoles -- use a tile's fullscreen for pixel-accurate control.

 -- Console Wall Plugin <noreply@example.com>  Sat, 25 Jul 2026 17:00:00 +0000

pve-console-wall (1.0.12) stable; urgency=medium

  * Show guest tags reliably (e.g. the "xen" tag). The PVEResources model does
    not always expose `tags` in record.data, so read it with a fallback to the
    raw API payload (record.raw.tags) in both the label overlay and the tag
    filter.

