pve-console-wall (1.0.9) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fix consoles not re-fitting in fullscreen. ExtJS does not re-run its layout
    when the element enters/leaves fullscreen, so tiles kept their old size.
    Force updateLayout()+relayout on fullscreenchange, and re-assert noVNC
    scaling whenever a tile is resized (tile onResize).

 -- Console Wall Plugin <noreply@example.com>  Sat, 25 Jul 2026 13:00:00 +0000

pve-console-wall (1.0.8) stable; urgency=medium

  * Console scaling and cursor alignment: replace the CSS object-fit hack (which
    offset the mouse) with noVNC's own Local Scaling, driven via its settings
    <select>. The console now zooms to fill the tile, centered, keeping aspect
    ratio, with correct mouse mapping.
  * Fix drag-to-reorder: console iframes swallowed drag/drop events. Disable
    iframe pointer events during a drag so drops reach the tile targets; also
    set a text/plain drag payload so the drag starts in all browsers.

 -- Console Wall Plugin <noreply@example.com>  Sat, 25 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000

pve-console-wall (1.0.7) stable; urgency=medium

  * Suppress the browser "changes you made may not be saved" (beforeunload)
    prompt on reload. Proxmox's noVNC console page registers a beforeunload
    handler; each console iframe is same-origin, so we neutralise it with a
    capturing listener that stops noVNC's and clear onbeforeunload.

