pve-console-wall (1.0.5) stable; urgency=medium

  * Console image now fits and centers in each tile. The embedded noVNC canvas
    rendered at native resolution top-left; inject same-origin CSS into the
    console iframe to scale the canvas (object-fit: contain, centered) and hide
    Proxmox's noVNC control-bar chrome. For pixel-accurate interaction use a
    tile's fullscreen button (opens Proxmox's native console).

 -- Console Wall Plugin <noreply@example.com>  Fri, 24 Jul 2026 23:00:00 +0000

pve-console-wall (1.0.4) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fix "noVNC failed to load" on Proxmox VE 9. novnc-pve ships only a bundled
    app.js (no importable core/rfb.js ES module), so the previous dynamic import
    could never resolve. Each console now embeds Proxmox's own noVNC console
    page in an iframe (/?console=...&novnc=1&vmid=...&node=...), reusing the
    native auth/ticket flow. Read-only mode disables iframe pointer events;
    reconnect reloads the frame. Version-independent.

 -- Console Wall Plugin <noreply@example.com>  Fri, 24 Jul 2026 22:00:00 +0000

pve-console-wall (1.0.3) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fix tiles rendering as thin stacked strips with no console area. The layout
    mixed CSS Grid with ExtJS's layout manager, and CSS forced height:auto and
    position:relative on tiles, collapsing them. Replaced with a JS layout
    engine (absolute positioning) that computes each tile's geometry — including
    hero spans for the 1+N styles — so ExtJS sizes the console bodies correctly.
    Tiles now re-flow on container resize.

 -- Console Wall Plugin <noreply@example.com>  Fri, 24 Jul 2026 20:00:00 +0000

pve-console-wall (1.0.2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fix blank Datacenter view (PVE 7/8/9). The datacenter-tree override
    captured and re-invoked me.callParent, which breaks ExtJS's parent-method
    chain and broke PVE.dc.Config construction. Reworked to override the base
    PVE.panel.Config.initComponent and append the Console Wall tab to me.items
    for the Datacenter instance only, using a normal callParent().

